From e9e8d0b877cf46f1b5725cc434e4e76a839b1f27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 05:46:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] test: cover the P2MR wallet fixes and the shared tree
 reconstruction

Unit tests: infer_script_tree_test pins InferTaprootTree() and InferP2MRTree()
against the same three shapes, since they now share one reconstruction helper.
It covers a complete unbalanced tree, two identical subtrees under the root,
whose leaves have identical control blocks, a tree missing a leaf, and a Merkle
root that does not belong to the output. tmr_max_depth_test accepts a tree 128
nesting levels deep, checks that its deepest leaf needs the full 4097 byte
control block, and refuses 129 levels. The descriptor cache comparison now also
compares tr_trees and p2mr_trees, not just the scripts and keys.

Functional tests: one depth-1 pk() P2MR input paying two P2WPKH outputs is
charged for, and really weighs, 590 weight units and 148 virtual bytes; a PSBT
signed without finalizing survives serialization and combining and then
finalizes, for SIGHASH_DEFAULT and for all six explicit types; a poisoned
second control block for a leaf does not prevent signing; a P2MR input cannot
be signed while another input of the same transaction has no spent output, and
signs as soon as one is supplied; signing falls through to a deeper leaf when
the shallow one is unsignable and prefers the cheapest control block when the
same leaf appears twice; and a single transaction spends P2MR together with
legacy, P2SH-SegWit, P2WPKH and P2TR inputs.
